{"type": "message", "id": "cd185149", "parentId": "7d92b9c9", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T12:29:49.508Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "chatcmpl-tool-afad98400506e9cf", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"deadliest cancers 5-year survival rate United States statistics\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1008,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e284b4c57590efc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Stat Facts: Common Cancer Sites - SEER\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e284b4c57590efc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/common.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa754b3e74e0d29e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n... Average annual percent change ... increasing trend and a negative AAPC a decreasing one. Cancer caused <strong>19.8% of all deaths in the United States in 2023</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa754b3e74e0d29e\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27fcf8f04a4efbdf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAL 30,030 AZ 42,560 AR 19,700 CA 199,980 CO 29,020 CT 23,920 DE 7,680 FL\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"27fcf8f04a4efbdf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/content/dam/cancer-org/research/cancer-facts-and-statistics/annual-cancer-facts-and-figures/2025/2025-cancer-facts-and-figures-acs.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6e9a6e7426f4d8cf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTable 8. Five-year Relative Survival Rates (%) by Stage at ... Figure 3. Leading Sites of New Cancer Cases and Deaths – ... Table 9. Incidence and Mortality Rates for Selected Cancers by ... Figure 4. Proportion of Cancer Cases and Deaths · Attributable to Cigarette Smoking in Adults 30 Years ... Figure 5.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6e9a6e7426f4d8cf\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2253347a8f308130\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nACS Annual Report: Cancer Mortality Continues to Drop Despite Rising Incidence in Women; Rates of New Diagnoses Under 65 Higher in Women Than Men\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2253347a8f308130\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pressroom.cancer.org/2025CancerFactsandFigures\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7dbb1d8b21d75d6b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn addition to projecting the contemporary cancer burden, ACS researchers compiled the most recent findings on population-based cancer occurrence and outcomes using incidence data collected by central cancer registries (through 2021) and mortality data collected by the National Center for Health Statistics (through 2022). The report also highlights lagging progress against pancreatic cancer, which is the third leading cause of cancer death in the U.S. Both incidence and mortality rates are increasing, and the five-year survival rate is just 8% for the 9 out of 10 people diagnosed with pancreatic exocrine tumors.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7dbb1d8b21d75d6b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pressroom.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78ab27778d7779b7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer Facts and Statistics | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"78ab27778d7779b7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/research/cancer-facts-statistics.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"870dba93056184e4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the United States, colorectal cancer is the 2nd most common cancer death overall and the leading cancer death in people under age 50 years. Colorectal Cancer Statistics 2026, published by the American Cancer Society flagship journal, CA: A Journal for Clinicians, provides the most recent statistics on colorectal cancer: ... African American and Black people have among the highest death rate and lowest survival of any racial/ethnic group in the US for most cancers.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"870dba93056184e4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8c52621590aaabb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer survival rates - Wikipedia\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e8c52621590aaabb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cancer_survival_rates\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bdefcdeb9eea7a6f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe 5-year relative survival rate drops to 22% for women with stage IV (metastatic) breast cancer. In cancer types with high survival rates, incidence is usually higher in the developed world, where longevity is also greater. Cancers with lower survival rates are more common in developing countries. The highest cancer survival rates are in countries such as South Korea, Japan, Israel, Australia, and the United States.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bdefcdeb9eea7a6f\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 31, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"en.wikipedia.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "deadliest cancers 5-year survival rate United States statistics", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 1008, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8e284b4c57590efc\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer Stat Facts: Common Cancer Sites - SEER\n<<<END_EXTER