{"type": "message", "id": "49c3c060", "parentId": "5983632a", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T12:30:40.019Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "chatcmpl-tool-aab9f9854dd36aeb", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"chordoma cases per year United States rare cancer incidence\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1019,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af06a2235bd7f9c8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: incidence and survival patterns in the United States, 1973-1995 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af06a2235bd7f9c8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11227920/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cce9e822991df053\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResults: The age-adjusted chordoma incidence rate (IR) of <strong>0.08 per 100,000</strong> was age-dependent, more common in males (IR 0.10) than females (IR 0.06) and rare among patients aged &lt;40 years and blacks.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cce9e822991df053\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"72a80bd771355fc3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: The Quest for Better Treatment Options - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"72a80bd771355fc3\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5315072/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4a2e9b2a294f9fd5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma is an extremely rare cancer, with an incidence of about <strong>one case per million persons per year</strong> in the USA and Europe (about 300 and 450 cases per year, respectively). The estimated 