{"type": "message", "id": "983225e3", "parentId": "ca4c0515", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T12:30:57.688Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "chatcmpl-tool-932b91fb28236897", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"meningioma brain tumor cases per year United States incidence\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1117,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15c4a6e2df48c665\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIncidence of Benign Meningiomas in the United States: Current and Future Trends - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15c4a6e2df48c665\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8160529/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"de1268011626cc02\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBenign meningiomas are the most frequently reported central nervous system tumors in the United States, with increasing incidence in past decades. However, the future trajectory of this neoplasm remains unclear. We analyzed benign meningioma incidence of cases identified by any means (eg, radiographically with or without microscopic confirmation) in US Surveillance, Epidemiology, and End Results cancer registries among groups aged 35 to 84 years during 2004-2017 by sex and race and ethnicity using age-period-cohort models.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"de1268011626cc02\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1cc7eb980d915936\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCBTRUS Fact Sheet - CBTRUS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1cc7eb980d915936\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://cbtrus.org/cbtrus-fact-sheet/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTR