{"type": "message", "id": "ad92feee", "parentId": "76d7a67a", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T12:31:05.280Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_342e1abf3cb84e2fbf46134f", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"uveal melanoma eye cancer cases per year United States incidence\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 999,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef33cfcb1abb4ab2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUveal melanoma: relatively rare but deadly cancer | Eye\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ef33cfcb1abb4ab2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nature.com/articles/eye2016275\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c78cd6524d04af93\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAlthough it is a relatively rare disease, primarily found in the Caucasian population, uveal melanoma is the most common primary intraocular tumor in adults with a mean age-adjusted incidence of <strong>5.1 cases per million per year</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c78cd6524d04af93\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 2, 2016\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nature.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b8d755641b6c60c5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nKey Statistics for Eye Cancer | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b8d755641b6c60c5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/eye-cancer/about/key-statistics.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b0a1718ea83428c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nMelanoma is the most common cancer of the eye and orbit in adults, but most melanomas (<strong>more than 9 out of 10)</strong> start in the skin.