 increase of 0.5% in uveal melanoma (the most common type of ocular melanoma) ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5b57f60e840f7d59\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6aa043ab0840f721\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAmbient ultraviolet radiation and ocular melanoma incidence in the United States, 2000−2019 | Eye\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"6aa043ab0840f721\">>>", "url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/s41433-024-02959-9", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a492f552cfbceda1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOcular melanoma is a rare, but deadly cancer. This large cancer registry study examines the associations between solar ultraviolet radiation (UVR) and incidence of different anatomical sites of ocular melanoma by sex, age, laterality, and race and ethnicity. Incidence data were derived from 21 cancer registries in the US for the years 2000–2019.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a492f552cfbceda1\">>>", "published": "February 13, 2024", "siteName": "www.nature.com"}]}, "isError": false, "timestamp": 1775737865280}}
{"type": "message", "id": "6714e97d", "parentId": "ad92feee", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T12:31:05.282Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_762bcd5974fb4d44888c9230", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"glioblastoma brain cancer cases per year United States 5-year survival rate\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 993,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4561770e5fb0abf5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEpidemiology and Outcome of Glioblastoma - Glioblastoma - NCBI Bookshelf\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4561770e5fb0abf5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470003/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd7db037872300cf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGlioblastoma (GBM) is the most ... up 54% of all gliomas and 16% of all primary brain tumors (2). GBM remains an incurable tumor with a <strong>median survival of only 15 months</strong> (3)....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"dd7db037872300cf\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"September 27, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9cfaa4d044197b1b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nReport Shows Adult Brain Tumor Incidence Rates are Decreasing but 5-Year Survival Rates Remain Low\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9cfaa4d044197b1b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pressroom.cancer.org/BrainTumorStats\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b07feb37b784ce72\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe slow progress largely reflects a lack of advancement in the early detection and treatment of glioblastoma, for which 5-year survival only increased from 4% to <strong>7%</strong> during this time period.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b07feb37b784ce72\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 24, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pressroom.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bc4a8a7e08871065\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGlioblastoma and Increased Survival with Longer Chemotherapy Duration - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bc4a8a7e08871065\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6710024/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a213e89afcbceb6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most prevalent locations of all brain tumors were the frontal lobe (25.6%) and the temporal lobe (19.6%). The CBTRUS also reported the mortality rate from malignant brain and CNS tumors was <strong>3.48 for females and 5.23 for males per 100,000 person-years</strong>. The five-year survival rate for GBM ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3a213e89afcbceb6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd393ce6c3420476\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGlioblastoma Survival Rate | Glioblastoma Foundation News\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd393ce6c3420476\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://glioblastomafoundation.org/news/glioblastoma-multiforme/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bf0dd654dbbf9170\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBecause of the infiltrative nature of glioblastoma and the lack of treatment advancement over the past 50 years, only about <strong>5 percent</strong> of glioblastoma patients survive more than five years, which means that doctors, researchers, and nonprofit ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bf0dd654dbbf9170\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 30, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"glioblastomafoundation.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"acdaaba5e3a36838\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhat is the average glioblastoma survival rate? — Glioblastoma Research Organization\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"acdaaba5e3a36838\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gbmresearch.org/blog/glioblastoma-survival-rate\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1264e50fde84e14c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChildren diagnosed with glioblastoma are predicted to have a better survival rate, and about <strong>25 percent</strong> of kids who have this tumor live for five years or more. A lack of data raises many questions about the most up-to-date information.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1264e50fde84e14c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 1, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.gbmresearch.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "glioblastoma brain cancer cases per year United States 5-year survival rate", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 993, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4561770e5fb0abf5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nEpidemiology and Outcome of Glioblastoma - Glioblastoma - NCBI Bookshelf\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4561770e5fb0abf5\">>>", "url": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK470003/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd7db037872300cf\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma (GBM) is the most ... up 54% of all gliomas and 16% of all primary brain tumors (2). GBM remains an incurable tumor with a <strong>median survival of only 15 months</strong> (3)....\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"dd7db037872300cf\">>>", "published": "September 27, 2017", "siteName": "www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9cfaa4d044197b1b\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n--