{"type": "message", "id": "9da90763", "parentId": "0415e355", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T12:31:34.190Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_ce6bc79d98144534bb31b5e6", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"brain cancer 5-year survival rate United States statistics glioblastoma\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 951,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b96863711c87f5b6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGlioblastoma and Increased Survival with Longer Chemotherapy Duration - PMC\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b96863711c87f5b6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6710024/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8471b91854767403\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe most prevalent locations of all brain tumors were the frontal lobe (25.6%) and the temporal lobe (19.6%). The CBTRUS also reported the mortality rate from malignant brain and CNS tumors was <strong>3.48 for females and 5.23 for males per 100,000 person-years</strong>. The five-year survival rate for GBM ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8471b91854767403\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5de5a4c0b086063f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nReport Shows Adult Brain Tumor Incidence Rates are Decreasing but 5-Year Survival Rates Remain Low\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5de5a4c0b086063f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pressroom.cancer.org/BrainTumorStats\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5cee5023426daab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nGlioblastoma accounts for <strong>49% of all malignant brain cancers in the U.S.</strong> Incidence rates for nonmalignant tumors, which disproportionately affect women and Black people, are slowly increasing, likely due to improvements in case finding and increased ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5cee5023426daab\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 24, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pressroom.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"14301bc42745c531\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSurvival Rates for Selected Adult Brain Tumors | American Cancer Society\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"14301bc42745c531\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/brain-spinal-cord-tumors-adults/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"89f77bfe08ff896f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor example, if the 5-year relative survival rate for a specific type of brain tumor is 70%, it means that people who have that tumor are, on average, <strong>about 70%</strong> as likely as people who don’t have that tumor to live for at least 5 years after being diagnosed.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"89f77bfe08ff896f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.cancer.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ca9b6d97f52637c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nCancer of the Brain and Other Nervous System - Cancer Stat Facts\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8ca9b6d97f52637c\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/brain.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6971b32224be9683\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn general, if the cancer is found ... other nervous system cancer, <strong>76.9% are diagnosed at the local stage. The 5-year relative survival for localized brain and other nervous system cancer is 35.3%</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6971b32224be9683\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"seer.cancer.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4f921e6d7671acb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nSurvival for Brain Cancer | Roswell Park Comprehensive Cancer Center - Buffalo, NY\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4f921e6d7671acb\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.roswellpark.org/cancer/brain/survival-rates\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4f0c776aae60ff7b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBrain cancer type. Survival varies widely among different tumor types. For example, 5-year relative survival for glioblastoma is <strong>5.7%</strong>, but for astrocytoma, the most common type of glioma, survival is 43.6%. For other gliomas, 5-year survival is 73.9%\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4f0c776aae60ff7b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.roswellpark.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "brain cancer 5-year survival rate United States statistics glioblastoma", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 951, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b96863711c87f5b6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma and Increased Survival with Longer Chemotherapy Duration - PMC\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"b96863711c87f5b6\">>>", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6710024/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8471b91854767403\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe most prevalent locations of all brain tumors were the frontal lobe (25.6%) and the temporal lobe (19.6%). The CBTRUS also reported the mortality rate from malignant brain and CNS tumors was <strong>3.48 for females and 5.23 for males per 100,000 person-years</strong>. The five-year survival rate for GBM ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8471b91854767403\">>>", "siteName": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5de5a4c0b086063f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nReport Shows Adult Brain Tumor Incidence Rates are Decreasing but 5-Year Survival Rates Remain Low\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"5de5a4c0b086063f\">>>", "url": "https://pressroom.cancer.org/BrainTumorStats", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5cee5023426daab\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nGlioblastoma accounts for <strong>49% of all malignant brain cancers in the U.S.</strong> Incidence rates for nonmalignant tumors, which disproportionately affect women and Black people, are slowly increasing, likely due to improvements in case finding and increased ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5cee5023426daab\">>>", "published": "August 24, 2021", "siteName": "pressroom.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"14301bc42745c531\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nSurvival Rates for Selected Adult Brain Tumors | American Cancer Society\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"14301bc42745c531\">>>", "url": "https://www.cancer.org/cancer/types/brain-spinal-cord-tumors-adults/detection-diagnosis-staging/survival-rates.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"89f77bfe08ff896f\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFor example, if the 5-year relative survival rate for a specific type of brain tumor is 70%, it means that people who have that tumor are, on average, <strong>about 70%</strong> as likely as people who don’t have that tumor to live for at least 5 years after being diagnosed.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"89f77bfe08ff896f\">>>", "siteName": "www.cancer.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ca9b6d97f52637c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nCancer of the Brain and Other Nervous System - Cancer Stat Facts\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8ca9b6d97f52637c\">>>", "url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/brain.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"697