{"type": "message", "id": "a49c03ae", "parentId": "8b0535eb", "timestamp": "2026-04-09T12:34:11.895Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Good data! I found:\n- Gallbladder cancer: ~12,640 new cases in 2026 (from American Cancer Society)\n- Overall cancer 5-year survival: 72.5%\n\nNow I need to finalize my lists. Let me think about what constitutes \"uncommon\" cancers. Gallbladder cancer with ~12,640 cases might be on the borderline. Let me look for truly rare cancers.\n\nFrom my research, I have:\n- Chordoma: ~300 cases per year\n- Adrenocortical carcinoma: ~300-400 cases per year\n- Hairy cell leukemia: ~700-1,300 cases per year\n- Uveal melanoma: ~1,700 cases per year\n\nI need one more. Let me search for another rare cancer.\n\nActually, let me also verify the lung cancer survival rate from SEER data.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_f3f674087a5e4acd97923ddf", "name": "web_fetch", "arguments": {"url": "https://seer.cancer.gov/statfacts/html/lungb.html"}}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_6297b5ec427740c89a0d46b5", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "mesothelioma cases per year United States rare cancer"}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "openrouter", "model": "z-ai/glm-5", "usage": {"input": 18816, "output": 405, "cacheRead": 13888, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 33109, "cost": {"input": 0.0112896, "output": 0.0007694999999999999, "cacheRead": 0.001652672, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0.013711772}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775738042081, "responseId": "gen-1775738042-lqAowoDRCx6Muk2IMS1T"}}
